From 3264b97a41927cf1d0f0e5d5182e08e069b572b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:42:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): lanes flow JSON, split landing steps, daily
 lane caps [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why: the lanes factory board needs one JSON for every open card's
step/reason/source and per-lane throughput, plus daily admission and
spend caps that hold new cards at the gate instead of guessing.

What:
- `hermes kanban lanes flow --json [--window 1h|6h|24h|7d]`
- steps intake/waiting/ready/running/review/ci/merge/deploy/test/done;
  unplaceable landing → landing_unclassified
- per-lane cards_per_day and usd_per_day (unset = unlimited), set via
  `lanes set`, reset at local midnight, reasons limit:cards_per_day /
  limit:usd_per_day

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_lanes_flow.py 33 passed;
test_kanban_lanes.py 41, test_kanban_lanes_plan.py 16,
test_kanban_lanes_tool_create.py 3, test_kanban_lane_order.py 13,
test_docs_drift.py 3; scripts/check --only health --base origin/main ok.
Live fleet replica snapshot: 145 open cards, 5 lanes.
